He's wrong.

192
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,640
And they're starting to find ways to condemn him.

193
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:29,840
And yet Nicodemus saw the amazing things that he did.

194
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:36,480
And so he goes to him at night and he says, uh, Hey teacher, um, please help me understand what's going on here.

195
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:40,800
And Jesus says to this guy who's arrived in religiosity.

196
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,920
And at this point has a good heart.

197
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:48,080
He says, ah, yeah, you got to be born again.

198
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:58,640
In fact, he says, unless you're born again, unless the spirit of God does something brand new in your spirit and bring your spirit back to life.

199
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:11,840
Uh, next winter, I'm hoping instead of going to Colorado, we'll go to somewhere like the Virgin Islands warm.

200
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:21,200
If you've ever gone snorkeling, you can stand out in this crystal clear water and you look around and you see ripples and you see that there's stuff down there.

201
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:23,920
You know, the things are going on.

202
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:35,680
You've been told the fish are beautiful, but until you put that mask on and you put your eyes down in the water and I mean, it's this unbelievable wonder.

203
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:39,600
Jesus says, that's what being born again is like.

204
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:48,240
That when you're, when you're born again, when you come into the kingdom, when you come into a relationship with God, all of a sudden the stuff you couldn't see.

205
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:53,060
What was the song we sang about his presence and that earth and heaven become one.

206
00:22:53,060 --> 00:23:00,880
I mean, it's, it is this sense of, I look and I all of a sudden see things that I had never seen before.

207
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,880
And it is an incredible season of wonder.

208
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:06,800
It's a season of delight.

209
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:09,840
It's, it's my testimony.

210
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:17,840
When I, when I met the Lord, I mean, I was, I had been seeking pleasure so much in my life that I think God had to show me that

211
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:21,080
abundant life that Jesus gave is better than what I was seeking.

212
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:23,780
And so he showed me that it could be better in pleasure too.

213
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:28,460
I remember walking across the campus of Penn State at college and, and blue sky.

214
00:23:28,460 --> 00:23:33,660
And I was praying and it just felt like God came and just gave me an unbelievable hug.

215
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:35,680
It was delight.

216
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:37,960
It was awesome.

217
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:45,120
Janet Hagberg wrote the critical journey.

218
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:52,420
Uh, she talks about the journey of faith and, and she says this about the beginning of the journey of faith.

219
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:58,440
She says, the recognition of God is where we all begin the journey of faith.

220
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:06,220
We may experience it during early childhood or as adults, regardless of our age.

221
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:12,220
However, it seems true that most begin the journey in a childlike way.

222
00:24:12,220 --> 00:24:23,700
We come to it with an innocence, a freshness that is seldom ever again as vivid or vital.

223
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:33,920
Someone has written that as wonderful as the season of delight and wonder is this, this first love.

224
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:36,760
It's still puppy dog love.

225
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:42,480
So the guys I hiked with, one guy was a third my age.

226
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:44,840
That's that guy all the way to the right.

227
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:46,360
Mark, great guy.

228
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:53,500
The, the part that bummed me out, he was like 104 pounds and his snowshoes were the same size as mine.

229
00:24:53,500 --> 00:24:57,140
If I ever do it again, I'm getting snowshoes that are like three times the size.

230
00:24:57,140 --> 00:25:01,640
Cause he would literally, he, he would just like dance across the top of the snow.

231
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:11,180
And I would go up this hill and I'd step and, and I mean, literally I did, you know, kick my snowshoe in to get a platform to be able to step up and kick it in again.

232
00:25:11,220 --> 00:25:22,680
And while he's just kind of wandering on up, great kid, uh, the guy taking the picture, he's in his twenties, loves the Lord, um, saw this trip as kind of an evangelistic opportunity for some of his friends.

233
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:31,000
But the guy in the middle, um, Deegan, this guy with the big beard, uh, we were about halfway up, but he didn't have his hood on.

234
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:36,520
Uh, he's 30 and he has this new girlfriend and he's just infatuated.

235
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:42,440
I mean, he's just in love, you know, she's in her twenties and, and oh, young love.

236
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:48,220
And I looked over at him and I go, Deegan, you got a big old hickey on your neck.

237
00:25:48,220 --> 00:25:52,080
His response was, yeah, you should see her.

238
00:25:52,080 --> 00:25:56,340
Any of you remember those days?

239
00:25:56,340 --> 00:25:59,080
I mean, I remember those days.

240
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:00,140
They were kind of fun.

241
00:26:00,140 --> 00:26:01,220
They were kind of exciting.

242
00:26:01,220 --> 00:26:05,420
Let me tell you, if I gave Lori a big hickey like that, now I'd get clobbered.

243
00:26:07,940 --> 00:26:16,300
Because it's this young love that is infatuating, it's, it's invigorating, it's enlivening, it's, it's wonderful, it's great.

244
00:26:16,300 --> 00:26:21,760
And you do stupid things like suck on each other's neck and give black and blue marks and you enjoy it.

245
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:28,020
It's a season of wonder, but be careful.

246
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:35,120
Be careful lest we normalize this season of wonder as the Christian experience.

247
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:41,920
Because when we do, and then we're not in it, we begin to look for a culprit.

248
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:54,640
We condemn ourselves, or we condemn God, or we condemn our spouse, or our family, or our boss, or our church, or our pastor.

249
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:59,960
Now I'm going to say this and I'm going to offend some of you, and so be it, because in a month I'll be gone.

250
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:06,720
You know, when I hear people say to me, you know, I'm not getting fed at my church anymore.

251
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:14,100
My response is, you know, in life, babies and really sick old people need fed.

252
00:27:14,100 --> 00:27:15,640
Which are you?

253
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:21,200
It's quiet.

254
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:24,000
Praise the Lord.

255
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:33,580
When we step out of the season of wonder, when God moves us from the season, and we're going to talk about that over the next couple weeks, what happens when we're in these other seasons.

256
00:27:33,580 --> 00:27:40,260
Just recognize that it might actually be the gift of God to form you into the image of Jesus in the ditch.

257
00:27:42,380 --> 00:27:44,520
Because what you want is to be more like Jesus.

258
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:50,680
Now, if what you want is just to be happy, that's okay, that's puppy dog love.

259
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:53,560
And there's nothing wrong with the season of wonder.

260
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:55,960
By the way, I'm back in it, and I love it, it's awesome.

261
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:59,380
I'll stay there as long as God will allow me.

262
00:27:59,380 --> 00:28:05,040
But ultimately, I don't want to be in the season of wonder, I want to be in the person of Jesus.

263
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:07,740
Wherever it is he's taking me.

264
00:28:07,740 --> 00:28:09,020
C.S. Lewis put it this way.

265
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:17,660
He said, our father refreshes us on the journey with some pleasant ends, but will not encourage us to mistake them for home.

266
00:28:17,660 --> 00:28:25,200
I think Dr. Terry Wardle says it as well as any one that I've heard.

267
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:30,240
When he said, the season of delight is sweet, innocent, exciting, and exhilarating.

268
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:38,420
In many ways, it could be compared to teenage puppy love that seems so complete, so deep, so permanent.

269
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:46,140
Christians would love to stay here forever, content to rest in the level of intimacy with God.

270
00:28:46,140 --> 00:28:50,640
It certainly feels new and alive and intoxicating.

271
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:55,000
But God will not allow Christians to remain there.

272
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,560
The journey will move on.

273
00:28:57,560 --> 00:29:00,400
The seasons will change.

274
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:07,480
The next season is a season where life is good, but God seems absent.

275
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:12,840
We've begun to do the things of God.

276
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:14,920
We're in a productive stage.

277
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:19,980
By the way, when I worked with pastors, a lot of pastors were in this place.

278
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:23,360
They knew how to do ministry.

279
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:25,480
They loved the word of God.

280
00:29:25,480 --> 00:29:26,900
They loved God.

281
00:29:26,900 --> 00:29:28,000
They loved the church.

282
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:31,340
And they liked the attention that they got being at the head of the church.

283
00:29:31,340 --> 00:29:33,300
They were productive.

284
00:29:37,100 --> 00:29:43,220
Unfortunately, in the midst of our productiveness, sometimes God says, yeah, so this is, if the

285
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:46,540
first one was, I can do this, this is the one I'm doing this.

286
00:29:46,540 --> 00:29:53,520
And when we get to the I'm doing this, sometimes God has to wean us from ourselves.

287
00:29:53,520 --> 00:30:00,060
I'm not going to say a lot about this, I think, next week.

288
00:30:00,060 --> 00:30:00,680
Is that right, Ryan?

289
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:04,380
Next week, Ryan is going to unpack this season for us.

290
00:30:04,380 --> 00:30:12,080
But just to tell you a quick story, there's a Hasidic Jewish leader, Rabbi Shuner Zalman.

291
00:30:12,080 --> 00:30:16,340
He was one of the initial leaders of the Hasidic movement.

292
00:30:16,340 --> 00:30:24,060
His son came home one day crying because he had been playing hide and seek out in the woods

293
00:30:24,060 --> 00:30:25,020
with the other boys.

294
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:31,020
And when he found a great place to hide, he sat there and all the other boys left and

295
00:30:31,020 --> 00:30:31,880
did something else.

296
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:40,220
So after finally realizing that no one was coming to find him, he came running home crying and

297
00:30:40,220 --> 00:30:43,040
told his dad the story of what had happened.

298
00:30:43,040 --> 00:30:51,180
To which the rabbi responded, ah, my son, that's how it is with God, too.

299
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:59,160
God is always hiding, hoping that people will come and look for him.

300
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:01,540
But no one wants to play.

301
00:31:01,540 --> 00:31:09,160
He's always left alone, waiting to be found, hoping someone will come, but crying because

302
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:10,520
no one seeks him out.

303
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:16,660
There's a lot to this season, and Ryan's going to do a great job.

304
00:31:16,660 --> 00:31:18,260
I just want to take one little piece.

305
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:21,960
And some of you have heard this before, so those who have, forgive me.

306
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:25,860
Do you know what object permanence is?

307
00:31:25,860 --> 00:31:29,100
Yeah, those who've been here know.

308
00:31:29,100 --> 00:31:34,940
So you show a baby an object, and what does the baby do?

309
00:31:34,940 --> 00:31:41,640
Because their primary mode of knowing is taste.

310
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:43,300
That's what they do.

311
00:31:43,900 --> 00:31:45,220
They touch it, they see it.

312
00:31:45,220 --> 00:31:52,160
But do you know that a baby only has an awareness of the object as long as the baby can perceive it?

313
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:57,000
As long as they can see it, touch it, taste it, feel it.

314
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:04,060
But the minute it's gone, in its own mind, the thing is gone.

315
00:32:05,940 --> 00:32:10,320
An infant has no capacity for object permanence.

316
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:18,680
And the way an infant gathers object permanence is the thing appears, and it's gone.

317
00:32:18,680 --> 00:32:20,760
And it appears, and it's gone.

318
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:22,700
And it appears, and it's gone.

319
00:32:22,700 --> 00:32:25,320
And at some point, the baby goes, oh!

320
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:29,700
Mom still exists when she leaves the room?

321
00:32:31,700 --> 00:32:32,140
No!

322
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:38,040
An object permanence gets embedded in their little brain that's being developed.

323
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:39,360
Well, here's the deal, folks.

324
00:32:39,360 --> 00:32:41,600
You're no different as Christians.

325
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:47,240
When God seems silent and absent.

326
00:32:47,240 --> 00:32:49,600
Now, notice it doesn't say God is absent.

327
00:32:49,600 --> 00:32:55,600
But when God seems absent, we begin to wonder, is he really there?

328
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:57,380
Was my faith true?

329
00:32:57,380 --> 00:33:00,380
Did all that stuff they taught me really make a difference?

330
00:33:00,380 --> 00:33:01,780
I mean, this stinks.

331
00:33:01,780 --> 00:33:03,300
I'm not even in the season of wonder anymore.

332
00:33:03,300 --> 00:33:05,800
And I've only, you know, the last two years have been awesome.

333
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:07,100
But man, O'Day, what's up with this?

334
00:33:07,100 --> 00:33:12,860
We did an Ash Wednesday service a year ago.

335
00:33:12,860 --> 00:33:15,760
And a good brother came up to me, and he was distraught.

336
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:19,360
Because the exercises we were doing, nothing was happening.

337
00:33:19,360 --> 00:33:22,160
Wasn't getting anything from it.

338
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:24,560
Began to ask, is there something wrong with me?

339
00:33:24,560 --> 00:33:25,780
Is there something wrong with the exercise?

340
00:33:25,780 --> 00:33:26,920
And the answer is no.

341
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:27,980
God's chosen silence.

342
00:33:27,980 --> 00:33:29,460
Why?

343
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:29,980
I don't know.

344
00:33:30,960 --> 00:33:35,800
But sometimes God builds an object permanence through silence.

345
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:40,800
Okay, I'll leave that to Ryan to take where he wants to go with it.

346
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:43,340
He'll do a great job, no doubt about that.

347
00:33:43,340 --> 00:33:45,540
Then there's a season of desert.

348
00:33:45,540 --> 00:33:47,500
Kent will be taking that the following week.

349
00:33:47,500 --> 00:33:49,120
Yeah.

350
00:33:49,120 --> 00:33:51,600
One person's excited.

351
00:33:51,600 --> 00:33:52,940
Which one of your children was that?

352
00:33:55,520 --> 00:33:59,920
That should take you a season of wonder for a little bit there, Kent.

353
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:00,420
That's good.

354
00:34:00,420 --> 00:34:05,160
Look, there's a lot of reasons why you can be in the desert.

355
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:10,100
The desert is a place where life is hard and God is present.

356
00:34:11,100 --> 00:34:13,700
I mean, you clearly see that in the Old Testament.

357
00:34:13,700 --> 00:34:19,200
You know, God takes them to the desert and they're whining, wanting their leeks and onions back from Egypt.

358
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:24,080
And yet God is so present, he's got a pillar of fire or a pillar of smoke, depending on whether it's day or night.

359
00:34:24,720 --> 00:34:27,640
But the presence of God is like, I want meat.

360
00:34:27,640 --> 00:34:29,920
I need water.

361
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:32,060
I mean, life was hard.

362
00:34:32,060 --> 00:34:34,600
And yet God was leading them.

363
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:39,560
And it's possible that you're in the desert because of sin.

364
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:40,280
Absolutely.

365
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:43,660
And if that's obvious to you, then what should you do?

366
00:34:43,660 --> 00:34:46,040
Repent.

367
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:49,280
Yeah, which means, okay, I'm going this way instead.

368
00:34:49,280 --> 00:34:50,440
I'm turning.

369
00:34:50,440 --> 00:35:01,020
But unfortunately, often we fail to see that each of these seasons can actually be God designed, a gift from God to develop something.

370
00:35:01,020 --> 00:35:10,380
Do you know that Jesus, Mark tells us, the spirit drove him into the, yeah, wilderness or the word there is desert.

371
00:35:10,380 --> 00:35:14,500
Did Jesus do anything wrong?

372
00:35:14,500 --> 00:35:16,460
Of course not.

373
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:22,340
Sometimes God has a plan to do something in the desert.

374
00:35:22,340 --> 00:35:33,160
And when we're lost in the desert, please, folks, don't let the evil one condemn you or tempt you to condemn God, your spouse, your boss, your church.

375
00:35:33,160 --> 00:35:38,080
You know, often there's this, yeah, I got a problem and you're it.

376
00:35:38,080 --> 00:35:39,640
No, no, no, no.

377
00:35:40,940 --> 00:35:42,620
Take some time and say, God, what are you doing?

378
00:35:42,620 --> 00:35:46,180
Rather than asking, how do I get out of the desert?

379
00:35:46,180 --> 00:35:48,860
Ask, what are you doing with me in the desert?

380
00:35:52,820 --> 00:35:56,240
So here's one of my favorite verses about the desert out of Hosea.

381
00:35:56,240 --> 00:36:02,740
God says to Israel, I am going to allure her.

382
00:36:02,740 --> 00:36:09,780
I'm going to lovingly woo her.

383
00:36:11,460 --> 00:36:16,520
I'm going to do it by leading her into the desert and speak tenderly to her.

384
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:20,220
You know, one of the realities of the desert is it strips you.

385
00:36:20,220 --> 00:36:21,800
All your distractions are gone.

386
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:26,820
Your painkillers are not available anymore to ignore the voice of God.

387
00:36:27,980 --> 00:36:37,200
The Desert Fathers, when Constantine Christianized the empire, first everybody was excited because all of a sudden evangelism worked.

388
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:40,420
Everyone came in and then they realized that people were coming in for the wrong reasons.

389
00:36:40,420 --> 00:36:42,640
And many of them weren't really believers.

390
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:46,200
And so people went out to the desert to seek God and to pray.

391
00:36:46,200 --> 00:36:48,220
And God, what's going on here?

392
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:52,820
This is the church that was pure and holy is now awful.

393
00:36:52,820 --> 00:36:54,620
What do we do?

394
00:36:54,900 --> 00:36:58,320
And when the Desert Fathers, they went into the desert, they went into the wilderness.

395
00:36:58,320 --> 00:37:00,180
The Spirit drove them into the wilderness.

396
00:37:00,180 --> 00:37:04,620
And they experienced a solitude with God.

397
00:37:04,620 --> 00:37:07,220
In the midst of that, one of the Desert Fathers said,

398
00:37:07,220 --> 00:37:11,160
when you go into the desert, don't expect to meet God.

399
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:14,700
Rather, expect to meet your demons.

400
00:37:14,700 --> 00:37:17,040
And they will be screaming.

401
00:37:17,040 --> 00:37:23,920
That at times, God will lead us to a place where we're forced to look at ourselves.

402
00:37:24,900 --> 00:37:37,840
We're forced to not have a phone, not have a TV, not have a person, not have a job, not have a religion to distract us from something God is doing in our life and heart.

403
00:37:37,840 --> 00:37:41,160
Again, Kent will do an amazing job with that.

404
00:37:41,160 --> 00:37:41,860
I have no doubt.

405
00:37:41,860 --> 00:37:44,240
And then the last one is darkness.

406
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:50,340
This is where life's hard and God's nowhere to be found.

407
00:37:50,340 --> 00:37:53,640
Now, he is, but I can't find him.

408
00:37:53,640 --> 00:37:56,220
He seems absent.

409
00:37:56,220 --> 00:38:01,120
And let me start by saying, I'm sure there are a few people here who are there.

410
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:10,360
And I want to apologize to you because Christians in the church often don't know how to handle this very well.

411
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:16,100
I've walked with a number of leaders who are in the desert.

412
00:38:17,500 --> 00:38:20,300
And it's a place of doubting.

413
00:38:20,300 --> 00:38:22,560
It's a place of questioning.

414
00:38:22,560 --> 00:38:26,580
It's a place of reorienting everything I thought I knew.

415
00:38:26,580 --> 00:38:30,180
